  "term": "voltage-gated ion channel",
  "definition": "A voltage-gated ion channel is a membrane channel whose activity changes with membrane voltage and helps control a cell’s electrical behavior. In the packet, these channels include sodium, calcium, and potassium channels involved in generating action potentials and regulating excitability.",
